From 22c6e559024264ddc05c225bfa02e0599e3c9baa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: friedger <mail@friedger.de>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:09:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] Belfry: send to someone from the directory, receive by
 QR, clearer history

Receive and Send on the wallet page are between participants: Send picks someone from the
Directory (kind-30078 opt-ins on the community relay, with name and picture; those whose wallet
has no 10019 yet are shown but cannot be chosen), or takes an npub or name@domain as before;
Receive shows a QR of <wallet>/?pay=<npub> that opens the payer's wallet (phone camera or the
wallet's scan button, which now recognises it) ready to send to this participant. Token strings
stay one tap further. History says "From your day pass", "From <name>" and "To <name>"
instead of "Ecash"; a line under the account explains the tokens; the Mints tab is hidden.
